From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:41:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] Take DispatchTime distances from the scheduler's own
 arithmetic

The polyfill called DispatchTime.distance(to:) where the release has it
(iOS 15, macOS 12). The SDK the armv7 build compiles against declares no
such method for the 5.4 Dispatch overlay the module is built with, so the
module did not typecheck, and a supplement declaring the method in the
module would shadow the system's own on every release. The polyfill's
arithmetic on rawValue is what every platform now runs.
---
 Sources/OpenCombineDispatch/DispatchQueue+Scheduler.swift | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Sources/OpenCombineDispatch/DispatchQueue+Scheduler.swift b/Sources/OpenCombineDispatch/DispatchQueue+Scheduler.swift
index 997a7be..276720d 100644
--- a/Sources/OpenCombineDispatch/DispatchQueue+Scheduler.swift
+++ b/Sources/OpenCombineDispatch/DispatchQueue+Scheduler.swift
@@ -266,11 +266,6 @@ private func clampedIntProduct(_ lhs: Int64, _ rhs: Int64) -> Int64 {
 extension DispatchTime {
 
     fileprivate func polyfillDistance(to other: DispatchTime) -> DispatchTimeInterval {
-#if canImport(Darwin) && compiler(>=5.1)
-        if #available(macOS 12.0, iOS 15.0, watchOS 8.0, tvOS 15.0, *) {
-            return distance(to: other)
-        }
-#endif
         let start = rawValue
         let end = other.rawValue
         if end >= start {
